],"choiceReasons":{"A":"**Towards** points in the station’s direction but does not guarantee that we reached it.","B":"Towards alone does not assert arrival.","C":"That would describe a static inside position, not direction.","D":"Away from gives the opposite direction."}}},{"id":"e8838ef9-d24a-5a39-aa19-4b0ec4dc0b73","topicSlug":"movement-prepositions","level":"A2","prompt":"Choose the route preposition: “We walked ____ the classroom.” The route is from outside to inside the classroom.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"beneath"},{"id":"B","text":"beside"},{"id":"C","text":"into"},{"id":"D","text":"above"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"Trace the **route described in words** before choosing the preposition.","explanation":"**into the classroom** expresses the specified route: from outside to inside the classroom.","keywords":["movement-route"],"skill":"movement-route","contextKey":"movement-prepositions-4","fingerprint":"3295cde22e33f281b3d8d43f6dfdcd7f57963a40b9633a957dc0bbf12240e656","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-prepositions-reference"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Trace the **route described in words** before choosing the preposition.","**into the classroom** expresses the specified route: from outside to inside the classroom.","Choose **into**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Beneath expresses a lower position, not this specified route.","B":"Beside expresses being next to it, not the described passage or crossing.","C":"**into the classroom** expresses the specified route: from outside to inside the classroom.","D":"Above expresses a higher position, not this specified route."}}},{"id":"a263a552-d32a-5dcc-a02a-3e2c360b478d","topicSlug":"movement-prepositions","level":"A2","prompt":"What route does “walk into the classroom” describe in this exercise?","choices":[{